{"nodes": [{"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_ruler_migration", "label": "70 \u2014 ruler migration: fold vectors, MCS re-run, tab:ladder re-score", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_gate_a", "label": "Gate A (decision row 87) \u2014 VENUE_SCALE_BASIS is the single authority", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_fold_vectors", "label": "eval/fold_vectors_L1_*.json", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The basis field was a hard-coded literal while values were already scored on the ruled basis, so Ellel's vectors carried a calendar_lag7 label on values that were not on that ruler; loss/secondary_loss are now written alongside a derived basis so a consumer cannot pair a MASE reader against an MAE vector."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_mcs_l1_results", "label": "eval/mcs_L1_results.json", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_tab_ladder", "label": "tab:ladder \u2014 the frozen six-origin committed gate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Deliberately not re-run at the later ceiling: doing so would replace the decision under audit with a different decision. It is not built from the per-fold vectors at all."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_tab_mcs", "label": "tab:mcs \u2014 which models the data cannot separate", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_ellel_naive_elimination", "label": "rung0_seasonal_naive eliminated from Ellel's 90% MCS", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "On the discredited ruler the seasonal-naive baseline could not be separated from the learned rungs at Ellel; on the ruled basis it can, which strengthens the ladder argument rather than weakening it."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_no_ranking_change_survives_se", "label": "No ranking change at any venue survives its own standard error", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The ruler change moves the level at Ellel and leaves the ordering undetermined among the leaders; a 1e-4 separation against a standard error of ~0.023 is a tie and must not be reported as a reordering."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_scoping_correction_tab_ladder", "label": "Scoping correction \u2014 these vectors are tab:mcs, not tab:ladder", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Carried through several sessions as 're-score tab:ladder'; reading the live Overleaf section settles it. The regenerated vectors feed tab:mcs."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_paired_design_variance_reduction", "label": "Pairing reduces the sd from 178.00 to 26.94", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A factor of 6.6, and the reason a 1.55 GBP gap is measurable at all \u2014 the paired design earning its place."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_fig_ladder", "label": "fig:ladder \u2014 three-panel per-venue distribution figure", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "MCS membership at alpha=0.10 is what the ink marks, because no ranking change survives its own standard error, so bolding a winner would be the W36 defect."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_guard_test_corrected", "label": "test_persisted_artefact_declares_its_overlap_and_scale_policy", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Asserted the same calendar_lag7 literal that let the mislabelling stand; now pairs on config.VENUE_SCALE_BASIS and asserts the loss field."}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_beer_hall", "label": "Beer Hall (anchor venue)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "brain/log/70_ruler_migration_rescore_result.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "brain_log_70_ruler_migration_rescore_result_ellel", "label": "Ellel (~82% zero days, ruled unscaled)", "file_type": "concept", "source_